title: $:/changenotes/5.5.0/#9872
description: Preserve additional blank lines as paragraph nodes
release: 5.5.0
tags: $:/tags/ChangeNote
change-type: feature
change-category: widget
github-links: https://github.com/TiddlyWiki/TiddlyWiki5/pull/9872
github-contributors: linonetwo

WikiText can optionally preserve additional blank lines as empty paragraph nodes, including leading and trailing blank lines and blank lines following block elements or inside containers. Each empty paragraph has a distinct source anchor, with support for LF and CRLF line endings. Enable this with the `preserveBlankLines` parser option or `$:/config/Parser/PreserveBlankLines`; the default parsing behaviour is unchanged. Vanilla gives the empty paragraphs visible height. Serializer support is maintained in the WikiText Serialize plugin.
